    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d355">

                <pb facs="0784" n="670" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg670"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Hull Papers</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The General Consultant</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Savage</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-08-12">August 12, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum</hi>
                </p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: It seems to me that further
                    consideration should be given two points in this memorandum for the President on
                    the subject of possible adherence of the French to the United Nations
                        Declaration.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d355-f1"/>
                </p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Under the Department’s announcement of January 5, 1942,<anchor n="2"
                            xml:id="d355-f2"/> adherence would not be to the Declaration but to its
                        principles. Presumably, this would not satisfy the French since they may
                        expect to be admitted as a full member under the final paragraph of the
                        Declaration.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>We have not taken any important step involving adherence without
                        consulting the British, Chinese, and Soviet Governments. According to the
                        attached memorandum, there would be consultation with the British
                        only.</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">arlton</hi>] S[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >avage</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d355-a1.xml" xpointer="d355-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d355-f1" n="1" xml:id="d355-f1-content">
                <p>i.e., the Declaration by United Nations, January 1, 1942. For text see Department
                    of the State, Executive Agreement Series No. 236; 55 Stat. (2) 1600; <ref target="frus1942v01#pg_25">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1942, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, pp. 25</ref>–<ref
                        target="frus1942v01#pg_26">26</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d355-f2" n="2" xml:id="d355-f2-content">
                <p>Quoted in the attachment to this memorandum, below.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
